# https://w3id.org/eudpp#CommonSpecification
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#CommonSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#CommonSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#TechnicalSpecification> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#CommonSpecification> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ESPR Art 42, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj#art_42"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#CommonSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Common specification means ecodesign requirements, essential requirements for digital product passports or test, measurement or calculation methods established by implementing acts adopted by the Commission for products covered by delegated acts pursuant to ESPR Article 4."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#CommonSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Common Specification"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityAssessmentModule
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityAssessmentModule> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityAssessmentModule> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Decision No 768/2008/EC Art 4, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec/2008/768(1)/oj#art_4"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityAssessmentModule> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ESPR Art 43, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj/#art_43"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityAssessmentModule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Conformity Assessment module means the possible conformity assessment elements that can be chosen, in accordance with certain criteria, to fullfill the conformity accessement required to be performed by Community harmonisation legislation in respect of a particular product."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityAssessmentModule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Conformity Assessment Module"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityCertificate
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityCertificate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityCertificate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Commission notice The ‘Blue Guide’ on the implementation of EU product rules 2022 Annex 4, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=oj:JOC_2022_247_R_0001"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityCertificate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ESPR Annex III (e)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityCertificate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Conformity assessment certificate for a certification. The blue guide uses the term \"cerficate of conformity\". The ESPR uses \"conformity certificate\" as well as \"certificate\" and \"approval decision\"."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityCertificate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Conformity Certificate"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#EUDeclarationOfConformity
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EUDeclarationOfConformity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EUDeclarationOfConformity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EUDeclarationOfConformity> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Decision No 768/2008/EC Annex I Art R10, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec/2008/768(1)/oj#anx_I"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EUDeclarationOfConformity> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ESPR Art 44, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj/#art_44"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EUDeclarationOfConformity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The EU Declaration of Conformity shall state that the fulfilment of the ecodesign requirements specified in the applicable delegated acts adopted pursuant to ESPR Article 4 has been demonstrated or that a presumption of conformity applies in accordance with ESPR Article 41."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EUDeclarationOfConformity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "EU Declaration of Conformity"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#HarmonisedStandard
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#HarmonisedStandard> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#HarmonisedStandard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ProductRequirement> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#HarmonisedStandard> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 Art 2 (1c), https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=celex%3A32012R1025#art_2"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#HarmonisedStandard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Harmonised Standard means a European standard adopted on the basis of a request made by the Commission for the application of Union harmonisation legislation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#HarmonisedStandard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Harmonised Standard"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#OtherTechnicalSpecification
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#OtherTechnicalSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#OtherTechnicalSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#TechnicalSpecification> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#OtherTechnicalSpecification> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ESPR Annex V, (6)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#OtherTechnicalSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Other technical specifications in relation to which conformity is declared."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#OtherTechnicalSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Other Technical Specification"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#ProductRequirement
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ProductRequirement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ProductRequirement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Product requirements means a requirement to be fullfilled by a product when placed on the market."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ProductRequirement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Product Requirement"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#TechnicalSpecification
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#TechnicalSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#TechnicalSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ProductRequirement> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#TechnicalSpecification> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 Art 2 (4)\nhttps://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=celex%3A32012R1025#art_2"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#TechnicalSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Technical specification means a document that prescribes technical requirements to be fulfilled by a product, process, service or system and which lays down one or more of the following: Common Specification or Other Technical Specification."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#TechnicalSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Technical Specification"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#UnionHarmonisationLegislation
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#UnionHarmonisationLegislation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#UnionHarmonisationLegislation> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Decision No 768/2008/EC Annex I Art R1 (17)\nhttps://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec/2008/768(1)/oj#anx_I"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#UnionHarmonisationLegislation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Union Harmonisation Legislation shall mean any Union legislation harmonising the conditions for the marketing of products. Examples are directives, regulations and delegated acts."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#UnionHarmonisationLegislation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Union Harmonised Legislation"@en .
